      "key": "agentic_conformance_diagnosis_and_gate",
      "statement": "Produced work must have correct change class, traceability and admission. A blocked walkthrough is a method defect only if a competent, correctly configured agent using declared authority cannot decide because an owning surface has ambiguity, missing step, contradiction or undecidable change class; reprice that defect into its owner. Ignoring authority, stale memory or bad reasoning is agent error; malformed artifacts are rejected either way. Runtime availability failures such as overloaded APIs/flaky transport cannot prove process soundness; walkthrough proof is runtime-independent. SPEC_METHOD/TICKETS own artifact rules for tickets, classifications, design derivations and execution contracts; this profile requires deterministic, fail-closed admission naming violated rules, not automatic truth for drafted classifications. Passed admission and walkthrough evidence do not ratify shared-method changes; repeated usage cannot constitutionalise grey work or amend the method.",
